{"step_index":204,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:23:13Z","input_tokens":2925,"cache_read_tokens":363375,"output_tokens":2868,"thinking":"The `inspect_b53_compositor.py` script provided key insights into the Blender 5.3.0 compositor nodes. Revealed are critical details about `CompositorNodeValToRGB`, `CompositorNodeMath`, and `CompositorNodeMix`. This data is essential for understanding the compositor's inner workings.\n\n\nInitial investigation revealed Blender 5.3.0 uses `ShaderNodeValToRGB`, `ShaderNodeMath`, and `ShaderNodeMix` instead of the assumed nodes. Specifically, `ShaderNodeMix` has distinct socket indexing when `data_type` is 'RGBA', warranting careful socket selection. The compositor nodes now include `ShaderNodeValue` and `ShaderNodeVectorMath` for the existing node set. Observing the outputs of `CompositorNodeRLayers` shows various data types: RGBA, VALUE, and VECTOR.\n\n\nInvestigating `CompositorNodeFilter` reveals potential for `'Sobel'` or `'Kirsch'` filter types, and `CompositorNodeTranslate` uses `'Clip'` for extension, potentially causing black borders; alternative options like `'Extend'` or `'Repeat'` might prevent this. Also examined `CompositorNodeCryptomatteV2` to confirm how the `matte_id` parameter can create accurate pixel masks for objects like the F1 race car.\n\n\nExamining the supported node types, it's clear `ShaderNodeTexCoord` isn't allowed, but `CompositorNodeImage` paired with `CompositorNodeScale` (with `Frame Type = Stretch`, `Crop`, or `Fit`) are natively supported.  The ability to generate or load textures like paper grain or radial speed lines directly through this combination opens up creative possibilities for the scene. Confirmation of paths shows the `v6_spiderverse/textures/*` directory is owned by the correct environment, enabling image loading.\n\n\nPacking images directly into the blend file avoids external dependencies and respects environment ownership boundaries. This ensures the availability of textures like radial speed lines and paper halftone within the scene. Confirmed this approach eliminates external file risks and enables rapid compositor evaluation for specific animation frames.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport bpy, time\n\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\LATEST\\v5_stage_anim.blend\")\nsc = bpy.context.scene\nsc.eevee.use_raytracing = False\nsc.eevee.taa_render_samples = 16\nsc.render.resolution_x = 1920\nsc.render.resolution_y = 1080\n\nvl = sc.view_layers[0]\nvl.use_pass_normal = True\nvl.use_pass_mist = True\nvl.use_pass_z = True\nvl.use_pass_emit = True\nvl.use_pass_cryptomatte_object = True\nsc.world.mist_settings.start = 12.0\nsc.world.mist_settings.depth = 160.0\n\nng = bpy.data.node_groups.new(\"BenchComp53\", 'CompositorNodeTree')\nrl = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeRLayers\")\nflt = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeFilter\")\nkuw = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeKuwahara\")\ntrn = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeTranslate\")\nscl = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeScale\")\ncry = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeCryptomatteV2\")\nmix = ng.nodes.new(\"ShaderNodeMix\")\nmix.data_type = 'RGBA'\n\nfor label, sock in [(\"Filter.Type\", flt.inputs['Type']),\n                    (\"Kuwahara.Type\", kuw.inputs['Type']),\n                    (\"Translate.ExtX\", trn.inputs['Extension X']),\n                    (\"Scale.Type\", scl.inputs['Type']),\n                    (\"Scale.FrameType\", scl.inputs['Frame Type'])]:\n    try:\n        sock.default_value = \"__INVALID__\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"ENUM {label}: {e}\")\n\nprint(\"Mix RGBA sockets:\", [(idx, s.name, s.type, s.enabled) for idx, s in enumerate(mix.inputs)], \"->\", [(idx, s.name, s.type, s.enabled) for idx, s in enumerate(mix.outputs)])\nprint(\"Cryptomatte props: source=\", cry.source, \"layer_name=\", cry.layer_name)\n\n# Wire a realistic full test chain: RLayers -> Kuwahara(Size=5) + Filter(Kirsch) + Sep/Translate/Comb + Output\nkuw.inputs['Size'].default_value = 5.0\nflt.inputs['Type'].default_value = 'Kirsch'\ntrn.inputs['Extension X'].default_value = 'Extend'\ntrn.inputs['Extension Y'].default_value = 'Extend'\ntrn.inputs['X'].default_value = 5.0\n\nsep = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeSeparateColor\")\ncmb = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeCombineColor\")\nng.links.new(rl.outputs['Image'], kuw.inputs['Image'])\nng.links.new(kuw.outputs['Image'], sep.inputs['Image'])\nng.links.new(rl.outputs['Image'], trn.inputs['Image'])\nsep2 = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeSeparateColor\")\nng.links.new(trn.outputs['Image'], sep2.inputs['Image'])\nng.links.new(sep2.outputs['Red'], cmb.inputs['Red'])\nng.links.new(sep.outputs['Green'], cmb.inputs['Green'])\nng.links.new(sep.outputs['Blue'], cmb.inputs['Blue'])\nng.links.new(sep.outputs['Alpha'], cmb.inputs['Alpha'])\n\nout = ng.nodes.new(\"NodeGroupOutput\")\nng.interface.new_socket(name=\"Image\", in_out='OUTPUT', socket_type='NodeSocketColor')\nng.links.new(cmb.outputs['Image'], out.inputs['Image'])\nsc.compositing_node_group = ng\nsc.use_nodes = True\n\nsc.frame_set(350)\nt0 = time.time()\nsc.render.filepath = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a98b6c71-b658-48ee-9b28-e9a1c116099c\\scratch\\bench_comp.jpg\"\nbpy.ops.render.render(write_still=True)\nt1 = time.time()\nsc.frame_set(700)\nbpy.ops.render.render(write_still=True)\nt2 = time.time()\nprint(f\"BENCH cold={t1-t0:.2f}s warm={t2-t1:.2f}s\")\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a98b6c71-b658-48ee-9b28-e9a1c116099c\\scratch\\inspect_b53_enums.py"}}]}
