{"step_index":210,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:24:34Z","input_tokens":2587,"cache_read_tokens":369331,"output_tokens":2446,"thinking":"The introspection output confirms the exact enum values and socket indices. This resolves the previous uncertainty about the data structures being used. The observed behavior appears consistent with the confirmed enum definitions.\n\n\nConfirmed the correct settings for various filter types including Kirsch and Anisotropic Kuwahara. The extension for translation is now set to extend, the scale type uses render size with a stretch frame. The shader node mix reveals a critical socket indexing issue where relying on string keys would incorrectly access disabled sockets, a helper function will ensure the correct inputs and outputs are always referenced.\n\n\nThe performance test of the Kirsch filter with RGB translation yielded promising results, suggesting parallel processing of the showcase clips is viable, potentially completing all frames within a few minutes. Also, a quick test of the Cryptomatte node is needed to confirm the matte output correctly isolates the hero car, particularly for the Spider-Verse quality scenes. The significance of an exact hero car Cryptomatte mask is hypothesized, especially considering its application in the painterly background effect and the misregistration mask.\n\n\nFocusing on the Cryptomatte matte, the goal is zero CMYK blur on the hero car, except during specific portal glitch frames. A depth-of-field-based off-focus mask will be applied, but the hero car matte will ensure the car remains sharp even in telephoto shots with significant depth and mist, maintaining its visual distinction from the background. The ink weight across different scales needs to be checked, especially in close-ups and telephoto shots to prevent the outlines from being too dark or disappearing. Also, the contrast across acts of the scene must be confirmed.\n\n\nThe scene's visual impact involves a split-screen effect with Spider-Verse misregistration and painterly brushstrokes on the background elements. An adaptive ink weight is implemented that attenuates screen-space edge ink on the car's matte at telephoto distances to prevent the edges from appearing too dark, while maintaining crispness in close-up shots. Specific duotone graphic impact frames will be created using the car matte and luminance data to generate stark inverted color flashes and graphic stencils.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport bpy, numpy as np\n\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\LATEST\\v5_stage_anim.blend\")\nsc = bpy.context.scene\nsc.eevee.use_raytracing = False\nsc.eevee.taa_render_samples = 8\nsc.render.resolution_x = 640\nsc.render.resolution_y = 360\n\nvl = sc.view_layers[0]\nvl.use_pass_cryptomatte_object = True\n\nrig = bpy.data.objects[\"RIG_F1_Race\"]\ncar_names = [o.name for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type in ('MESH', 'CURVE') and (o.parent == rig or o.name.startswith((\"GEO_F1_\", \"GEO_MERC_\", \"DEC_\")))]\n\nng = bpy.data.node_groups.new(\"TestCrypto\", 'CompositorNodeTree')\ncry = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeCryptomatteV2\")\ncry.source = 'RENDER'\ncry.scene = sc\ncry.layer_name = f\"{vl.name}.CryptoObject\"\ncry.matte_id = \",\".join(car_names)\n\nout = ng.nodes.new(\"NodeGroupOutput\")\nng.interface.new_socket(name=\"Image\", in_out='OUTPUT', socket_type='NodeSocketColor')\n# Output Matte as grayscale image to verify coverage\ncmb = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeCombineColor\")\nng.links.new(cry.outputs['Matte'], cmb.inputs['Red'])\nng.links.new(cry.outputs['Matte'], cmb.inputs['Green'])\nng.links.new(cry.outputs['Matte'], cmb.inputs['Blue'])\ncmb.inputs['Alpha'].default_value = 1.0\nng.links.new(cmb.outputs['Image'], out.inputs['Image'])\n\nsc.compositing_node_group = ng\nsc.use_nodes = True\nsc.view_settings.view_transform = 'Standard'\nsc.view_settings.exposure = 0.0\n\nmks = sorted(sc.timeline_markers, key=lambda m: m.frame)\nsc.camera = [m.camera for m in mks if m.frame <= 520][-1]\nsc.frame_set(520)\nout_p = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a98b6c71-b658-48ee-9b28-e9a1c116099c\\scratch\\crypto_matte_test.png\"\nsc.render.image_settings.file_format = 'PNG'\nsc.render.filepath = out_p\nbpy.ops.render.render(write_still=True)\n\nim = bpy.data.images.load(out_p)\npx = np.array(im.pixels[:]).reshape((360, 640, 4))[..., 0]\nprint(f\"Crypto matte @ f=520: min={px.min():.3f} max={px.max():.3f} car_area_pct={(px > 0.5).mean()*100:.2f}% str_len={len(cry.matte_id)}\")\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a98b6c71-b658-48ee-9b28-e9a1c116099c\\scratch\\test_cryptomatte.py"}}]}
